{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1427863-ex3-so-far","id":1427863,"title":"EX3 So Far","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-12-09T08:41:23-08:00","id":1427863,"title":"EX3 So Far","content":"It seems like the EX3 Development is frozen for many month. I know there's a lot of topics like this one but I'm really waiting for the next EX3 Kickstarter's (Exigent I suppose ?). In fact I'm really (really) waiting for Exalted Essence more than Exigent.<br /> <br /> Any good news on the way or should I go on with depression ? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Sorry if that topics looks like another complaint about the speed development because it's not","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12575-gaara","name":"Gaara","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-09T08:46:24-08:00","id":1427864,"title":"","content":"I figure that the Exigents Kickstarter will be Soon (tm), and I'm pretty sure it was supposed to happen this past year but-<br /> <br /> *Looks at Covid and all of 2020*<br /> <br /> Y'know, Things Happen. :P<br /> <br /> Edit: Also, the development has still been happening to the best of their ability (checking the progress on the Monday Meeting Notes) so it's not like the freelancers have been sitting on their thumbs this whole time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 12-09-2020, 11:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-09T09:28:00-08:00","id":1427871,"title":"","content":"They're talking visuals for Essence, as of the latest Monday Meeting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-09T13:12:34-08:00","id":1427897,"title":"","content":"I dunno. People talk about Covid, but Onyx Path ran seven KSes in 2020, which is a new record (it was six each for the past two years).<br /> <br /> Also, don't get too stuck on the idea of Exigents being &quot;soon&quot; in any useful sense. It's really hard to deduce much from the stages of development, but it's relatively consistent that things enter art direction at least 3-4 months before they get KS'd, and Exigents hasn't, implying mid-2021 would be the earliest reasonable guess, likely later.<br /> <br /> Essence Edition is now in art direction, though admittedly with a much more &quot;early stage&quot; description that most things get as their first update, so we could optimistically hope for it in April or May.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-09T13:15:33-08:00","id":1427898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1427863-ex3-so-far?p=1427897#post1427897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dunno. People talk about Covid, but Onyx Path ran seven KSes in 2020, which is a new record (it was six each for the past two years).</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Rich said members of the Exalted team were hit harder than most. Like if an ex3 dev lost their day job and a family member to the virus it would have an imbalanced impact on Onyx Path releases.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-09T13:29:52-08:00","id":1427899,"title":"","content":"Certainly true. And my thoughts are with the Exalted team in whatever those struggles are.<br /> <br /> I just want to underline that Exalted's situation is unusual, rather than filing it under &quot;you know, 2020.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-09T13:43:21-08:00","id":1427900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1427863-ex3-so-far?p=1427897#post1427897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, don't get too stuck on the idea of Exigents being &quot;soon&quot; in any useful sense. It's really hard to deduce much from the stages of development, but it's relatively consistent that things enter art direction at least 3-4 months before they get KS'd, and Exigents hasn't, implying mid-2021 would be the earliest reasonable guess, likely later.</div> </div> </div> </div>When I say 'Soon (tm)' I actually mean &quot;Sometime before the heat death of the universe&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-09T15:08:52-08:00","id":1427911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1427863-ex3-so-far?p=1427899#post1427899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just want to underline that Exalted's situation is unusual, rather than filing it under &quot;you know, 2020.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>It's less unusual and more that the gameline drew the short straw. If Matthew Dawkins or Travis Legge had been hit hard by COVID, it could have easily pushed back projects that happened this year.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-09T19:51:31-08:00","id":1427937,"title":"","content":"The <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?filters=0_0_45735_0_45643_0_0&amp;src=fid45643&amp;page=1&amp;sort=4a\" target=\"_blank\">storyteller's vault</a> has some Exalted products that might patch you through the drought. Lower quality, but cheaper and releases more often.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-10T01:05:21-08:00","id":1427946,"title":"","content":"I mean it's really not frozen, it's just running cold, like it always did. It's a small team terrified of releasing a product of 2e quality, so they take pretty long. Always has been this slow, and I've gotten used to it. We got Lunars, Dragon Blooded and Solars released, so really there's nothing stopping us from running proper campaigns right now.<br /> Admittedly, I really want At8D, but who doesn't?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/903-cheshire-cat","name":"Cheshire Cat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar903_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-10T05:32:48-08:00","id":1427960,"title":"","content":"And production at OPP just runs a low slower than it did back in the old days of White Wolf. The second edition of Chronicles of Darkness is around 8 years old, and they still haven't released books for all of the 1st edition lines. Gone are the days of an office full of writers, drop dead dates with printers, and a publication calendar to meet. It's just the nature of the business. Look how much trouble Paradox has had getting V5 off the ground. It's been over 2 years, and they haven't even released all the clans yet, and that's with a bigger wallet than OPP is working with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-10T07:14:57-08:00","id":1427971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1427863-ex3-so-far?p=1427898#post1427898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think Rich said members of the Exalted team were hit harder than most. Like if an ex3 dev lost their day job and a family member to the virus it would have an imbalanced impact on Onyx Path releases.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sorry about that <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. I didn't know. I just believed Covid didn't slow developer as Kickstarter of other products from OP goes on. But teams members are not the same. My thoughts to all people affected by this &quot;looks like Great Contagion&quot; Covid<br /> <br /> Also I understand the 2nd Edition experience and the will to do better balanced products<br /> <br /> Thank you all","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12575,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12575-gaara","user":"Gaara","date":". 12-10-2020, 10:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12575-gaara","name":"Gaara","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-10T07:59:43-08:00","id":1427976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1427863-ex3-so-far?p=1427960#post1427960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And production at OPP just runs a low slower than it did back in the old days of White Wolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, this is true, but incomplete. Even before Covid (&quot;BC&quot;?), Exalted was running slower than other OPP properties. I think that's because of the very crunchy nature of the rules, though since it also seems to have caused trouble for Across the Eight Directions (happy second birthday to that book), there are clearly other factors at work as well.<br /> <br /> Maybe it's the extra research needed for a setting as unique and diverse as Creation? Or the need to consider all the ways things have been previous portrayed in the line?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-10T08:26:41-08:00","id":1427979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1427863-ex3-so-far?p=1427976#post1427976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, this is true, but incomplete. Even before Covid (&quot;BC&quot;?), Exalted was running slower than other OPP properties. I think that's because of the very crunchy nature of the rules, though since it also seems to have caused trouble for Across the Eight Directions (happy second birthday to that book), there are clearly other factors at work as well.<br /> <br /> Maybe it's the extra research needed for a setting as unique and diverse as Creation? Or the need to consider all the ways things have been previous portrayed in the line?</div> </div> </div> </div>Kind of context matters a bit. Scion was supposed to be KS'd in 2013 along with Exalted 3e, and that didn't happen until what? 2018? AndMage: the Awakening 2e has had <b>Secrets of the Pentacle</b> in development hell for years now. Exalted had a slower start, but at this moment actually does have more releases than many other OPP games have since htey started KSes, and they also have I think some of the most on the docket when I go through my notes for Exalted, TC, and Scion at least. Like, Masks of the Mythosand <b>Scion: Dragon</b> were annoucned in January last year, and are probably gonna KS next year. So to me at least, generally the perception of Exalted as slow is mostly a result of the KS and the slow start even when 3e landed. The current devs do move things along more.<br /> <br /> In that context, 2020 derailing seems pretty likely and more or less has been what aformentioend current devs and writers have said. More that would have been out htis year couldn't get out this year and htis is why we got hte <b>Heirs to the Shogunate</b> preview.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-10T09:27:54-08:00","id":1427993,"title":"","content":"Maybe it's also because between Lunars and Exigent, the developers changed their minds and wanted to release their final products next to the Kickstater's finish line ?<br /> So maybe we could hope Exigent KS in the begining of 2021 and the printed book in mid (or end) 2021 ?<br /> <br /> I'm pretty sure having read about that no ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12575-gaara","name":"Gaara","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-10T10:25:41-08:00","id":1428007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaara</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1427863-ex3-so-far?p=1427993#post1427993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe it's also because between Lunars and Exigent, the developers changed their minds and wanted to release their final products next to the Kickstater's finish line ?<br /> So maybe we could hope Exigent KS in the begining of 2021 and the printed book in mid (or end) 2021 ?<br /> <br /> I'm pretty sure having read about that no ?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't remember anything to that extent. Lunars more or less came out about on pace theyw anted for these, they just knew Exigents woudl beharder and this year in general maeks that harder.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-10T10:52:01-08:00","id":1428010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaara</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1427863-ex3-so-far?p=1427993#post1427993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe it's also because between Lunars and Exigent, the developers changed their minds and wanted to release their final products next to the Kickstater's finish line ?<br /> So maybe we could hope Exigent KS in the begining of 2021 and the printed book in mid (or end) 2021 ?<br /> <br /> I'm pretty sure having read about that no ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing like that is happening. <i>Exigents</i> development is simply running slow; the manuscript will be in roughly the same place when we Kickstart it as the <i>Lunars</i> manuscript was.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-10T21:11:18-08:00","id":1428050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1427863-ex3-so-far?p=1427976#post1427976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, this is true, but incomplete. Even before Covid (&amp;quot;BC&amp;quot;?), Exalted was running slower than other OPP properties. I think that's because of the very crunchy nature of the rules, though since it also seems to have caused trouble for Across the Eight Directions (happy second birthday to that book), there are clearly other factors at work as well.<br /> <br /> Maybe it's the extra research needed for a setting as unique and diverse as Creation? Or the need to consider all the ways things have been previous portrayed in the line?</div> </div> </div> </div>We're also a year out from the final monthly release, which seems to be trapped in the same limbo even though it's been in development for as long if not longer","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-11T08:43:36-08:00","id":1428095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SamuraiMujuru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1427863-ex3-so-far?p=1428050#post1428050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We're also a year out from the final monthly release, which seems to be trapped in the same limbo even though it's been in development for as long if not longer</div> </div> </div> </div>Rich said that there is more content in the compilation book they are working on. I dunno how much in a way of new things are being added though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>--Lurker Extraordinaire!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/344-darkwolff","name":"DarkWolff","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-11T10:14:14-08:00","id":1428105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkWolff</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1427863-ex3-so-far?p=1428095#post1428095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Rich said that there is more content in the compilation book they are working on. I dunno how much in a way of new things are being added though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, but the pitch was always &quot;we'll stop the monthly content when the rest of the book is complete and release is imminent-ish&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-15T07:43:42-08:00","id":1428472,"title":"","content":"For folks that don't read the MMN, this was a substantial chunk of it this week along with a number of Exalted projects finally moving up in production. .<br /> <br /> &quot;&quot;If you start with last Monday\u2019s meeting, then last week\u2019s production meeting, and then today\u2019s meeting, our biggest ongoing conversation was about Exalted. We started reviewing just how our plans for it were hammered by everything that happened in 2020. It is no exaggeration to say that every project and every creator was affected, and then all of our outside partners like our printers and shippers were also delayed and understaffed by what went on.<br /> <br /> That was the background, the what was. We needed that to get to just what we were doing about getting Exalted as a game line back on track. (And please do be aware that we all know that this is a conversation we have had several times before. We know, oh we know.) Last week, we heard those plans to accelerate the release schedule heading into 2021, this week we saw them implemented. The start is something you too can look at in the Project Status Updates, below.<br /> <br /> It is the start. And here\u2019s Dixie Cochran with a bit more info as she has been the person boosting and holding the team together all through all this:<br /> <br /> Hi, Exalted fans!<br /> <br /> <br /> I know it\u2019s been a bit since anything came out for the line, and I\u2019m sorry it\u2019s been slow. 2020 hit our team a little harder than a lot of the others, to be perfectly honest. We\u2019ve had illnesses, family emergencies, and some people working 12-hour workdays or picking up the work of three people in their day jobs. This is, of course, on top of everything (pandemic, protests, anxiety, etc.) this past year has brought in general.<br /> <br /> <br /> That said, I think 2021 is going to be a banner year for Exalted Third Edition! In addition to the deluxe version of Lunars: Fangs at the Gate being on the way soon, art is rolling in for Heirs to the Shogunate, and it\u2019s lovely. This week, we have movement on both Hundred Devils Night Parade and Exalted Essence, the latter of which I\u2019m looking over before we send it on to Paradox.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve been assured Across the Eight Directions will be in my hands shortly, even with the aforementioned 12-hour days one of the devs is dealing with. We\u2019re aiming for about a month from now to have Many-Faced Strangers off to approvals, with Adversaries of the Righteous before that. The player\u2019s guide, Crucible of Legend, should also be off to approvals by the end of this year.<br /> <br /> Additionally, we\u2019ve brought on two new developers over the past few months to help move things along. One of them is working on Exigents, which we\u2019re hoping to see completed and approved by the end of Q1 or the beginning of Q2 2021. The other has been assisting on HDNP and AotR, as well as developing Many-Faced Strangers and Across the Eight Directions.<br /> <br /> So yeah, 2020 was a bit of a bust all around (though I was and continue to be so happy with the reaction to the PoD and PDF of Lunars on DriveThruRPG).<br /> <br /> Here\u2019s to 2021 being a truly Exalted year!<br /> <br /> As always, thank you to our developers, writers, artists, layout people, editors, and (most importantly) you, the fans! We know you\u2019re hungry for more content and we can\u2019t wait to show you what we\u2019ve been working on.<br /> <br /> So say we all!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-17T06:04:09-08:00","id":1428742,"title":"","content":"That's sounds great. 2021 will be an Exalted's year off for my players and I because we're aiming to finish our L5R campaign. But it would be a perfect timing to have a lot of new Exalted's stuff in 2021 to help me creating the next chapter of the current campaign I run","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12575-gaara","name":"Gaara","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}